INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft / CISA advisory mirror", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a", "text": "SRC-001 deep-search content: Mandiant reported on June 2, 2023 that Progress announced the MOVEit Transfer vulnerability on May 31, 2023 and it was assigned CVE-2023-34362. Earliest observed exploitation was May 27, 2023, involving deployment of web shells and data theft; some theft occurred within minutes. On June 6, the CL0P^_-LEAKS data leak site claimed responsibility and threatened to publish stolen data unless an extortion fee was paid. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate, and data leak site overlaps. Actors deployed a newly discovered C# LEMURLOOT web shell, often masquerading as human.aspx, with observed variants human2.aspx and _human2.aspx. POST requests to guestaccess.aspx preceded webshell interaction, indicating SQL injection attacks directed at that file. LEMURLOOT could enumerate files/folders, retrieve configuration, create/delete a hard-coded Health Check Service user, download files, and extract Azure Blob storage settings/credentials. Large volumes of files were stolen in multiple cases. Scanning/exploitation often came from 5.252.188.0/22, while webshell interaction/data theft came from different systems. Many second-stage hosts exposed RDP and certificates generated May 19-22, suggesting staging. Mandiant identified overlaps in ISPs, netblocks and IP addresses with historical FIN11 operations; an IP attempting CVE exploitation had been used by FIN11 as early as mid-January 2023, hosting RDP on TCP 3389 and presenting the same x509 certificate when UNC4857 began using it. On June 5 Bleeping Computer reported an alleged CLOP-affiliated statement; on June 6 the CL0P^_-LEAKS site claimed responsibility. Mandiant had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims and said delayed ransom emails were plausible based on prior FIN11 behavior. FIN11 had previously conducted data-theft extortion after exploiting Accellion FTA (DEWMODE webshell) and GoAnywhere MFT CVE-2023-0669. The source labels the activity as consistent with extortion actors, but some links remain attribution assessments."}
